.TH BODYHASH 1 "2026-11-11" "bodyhash 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bodyhash \- hash a file body, excluding marked regions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bodyhash
.BR hash | check | markers
.I FILE
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bodyhash
computes a hash of file content, excluding any regions delimited by
user-specified marker pairs. By default, it normalizes line endings, strips
UTF-8 BOM, and removes trailing whitespace to ensure consistent hashes
across different operating systems and editors.
.PP
Every requested \fI\-\-exclude\fR pair must be found in the file, and every
START must be closed by its END; otherwise
.B bodyhash
fails with exit code 3 instead of silently hashing a truncated body.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B hash
Output the hash of the file body.
.TP
.B check
Compare the file body hash with an expected value (case-insensitive).
Exits 0 if they match, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.B markers
Display the line numbers where the specified markers are found.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exclude =\fISTART::END\fR
Exclude every block delimited by the literal markers \fISTART\fR and
\fIEND\fR (both boundary lines are excluded). The pair is split on the
first "::"; markers may not contain "::" and must be non-empty.
This option can be used multiple times.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-algo =\fIALGO\fR
Specify the hash algorithm. Supported: \fBsha256\fR (default), \fBsha512\fR,
\fBmd5\fR, \fBblake2b\fR, \fBblake2s\fR, \fBsha3-256\fR, \fBsha3-512\fR.
The hashing backend is auto-detected: \fIsha256sum\fR/\fIsha512sum\fR/\fImd5sum\fR/\fIb2sum\fR
(GNU), then \fIshasum\fR/\fImd5\fR (BSD/macOS), then \fIopenssl dgst\fR
(the only backend for \fBsha3-*\fR and \fBblake2s\fR). All backends produce
identical digests for the same algorithm.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-normalize\-crlf
Do not convert CRLF/CR to LF. By default, line endings are normalized.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-strip\-bom
Do not strip the UTF-8 BOM (Byte Order Mark) from the beginning of the file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-strip\-trailing\-ws
Do not remove trailing whitespace from each line before hashing.
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-trailing\-ws
Strip trailing whitespace (default).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-strip\-leading\-ws
Keep leading whitespace (default).
.TP
.B \-\-strip\-leading\-ws
Remove leading whitespace from each line before hashing.
.TP
.B \-\-indent\-tabs=\fIN\fR
Expand tab characters to the next multiple of \fIN\fR columns before
hashing. Uses \fIexpand\fR when available, otherwise a built-in awk
fallback with the same tab-stop math. \fIN\fR must be a positive integer.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-preamble
Skip the content before the first START marker.
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-epilogue
Skip the content after the last END marker.
.TP
.B \-\-strict\-start
Fail if the first START marker is not on line 1 (exit code 2).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output (e.g., print OK on successful check).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the verbose OK message; errors are still printed.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success (hash matched).
.TP
.B 1
Hash mismatch (check command only).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments: unknown option, malformed \fISTART::END\fR, invalid
\fI\-\-indent\-tabs\fR value, or strict-start failure.
.TP
.B 3
Marker pair not found: START missing, END missing (unterminated block),
or a repeated \fI\-e\fR pair absent from the file.
.TP
.B 4
File not found.
.TP
.B 5
Internal error (e.g., hasher produced no output).
.TP
.B 6
Unsupported algorithm, or no hashing tool available for it.
.SH NOTES
The tool is locale-independent: awk and grep are always invoked with
.B LC_ALL=C
(byte semantics), so hashes are identical regardless of the system locale
and the awk implementation (gawk, mawk, BSD awk, busybox awk). In
particular, the UTF-8 BOM is stripped correctly even in UTF-8 locales,
where gawk would otherwise treat it as a single character.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Hash the body of a C file, excluding the Doxygen header:
.EX
bodyhash hash file.c \-e '/**::*/'
.EE
.TP
Verify the hash against a known value:
.EX
bodyhash check file.c 1857616f15bd53f72c1733a1839421116c7bbb50579f2cdb9ceca9adfcd30fda \-e '/**::*/'
.EE
.TP
Exclude a metadata header and a volatile block at once:
.EX
bodyhash hash file.conf \-e '[META::[/META]' \-e '<volatile::</volatile>'
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sha256sum (1),
.BR shasum (1),
.BR openssl (1)
